===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
Originally {{Han compound|ls=psc|殄|貝|c1=p|c2=s|t2=cowry|alt1=𠂈|nocap=yes}}; 𠂈 (a knife or dagger) was then a phonetic component. Often {{och-l|丁}} (a nail) was added as a second phonetic component at the bottom; originally, it appeared as a black dot. {{zh-ref|He Linyi}} posits it to be the original character for {{och-l|珍|rare; valuable}}.

The sound component {{zh-l|*𠂈}} corrupted into {{zh-l|*十}} in the modern form, and into {{zh-l|*匕}} in the orthodox seal script form {{zh-l|*眞}}. The bottom of the character in both forms derives from the components {{zh-l|*貝}} and {{zh-l|*丁}} corrupting into {{zh-l|*目}} and {{zh-l|*丌}}.

===Etymology===
From {{der|zh|sit-pro|-}}; cognate with {{cog|bo|བདེན||true; truth}}. Possibly connected with {{och-l|貞}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

