===Glyph origin===
Corrupted variant of {{l|zh|著}} ({{l|zh|艹}} → {{l|zh|䒑}}; {{l|zh|日}} → {{l|zh|目}}). Recorded as an unorthodox form ({{zh-l|俗字*}}) in the {{w|Tang dynasty}} orthographic dictionary ''{{w|Ganlu Zishu}}'' {{lw|zh|pref=《|干祿字書|suf=》}}. <!-- Refer http://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/variants/rbt/word_attribute.rbt?educode=A03506-015#18 -->

Later dictionaries such as the {{w|Ming dynasty}} {{lang|zh|《字學三正》}} and {{w|Qing dynasty}} ''{{w|Zhengzitong}}'' {{lw|zh|pref=《|正字通|suf=》}} recorded the glyph as {{lang|zh|⿱𦍌⿰丿目}}.

===Definitions===
{{zh-see|著}}

===Usage notes===
{{lang|zh|sc=Hant|着}} is both the standard and variant traditional character of some senses of {{zh-l|*著}} (Pronunciations 1 and 2). In Hong Kong, {{lang|zh|sc=Hant|着}}(zoek3/zoek6) and {{lang|zh|sc=Hant|著}}(zyu3) are both used and represent different meanings.

In mainland China's {{w|Table of General Standard Chinese Characters}} ({{lw|zh|通用规范汉字表}}), {{l|zh|著|tr=zhù}} is not listed as a traditional form of {{lang|zh|sc=Hans|着}} and is considered a separate character. <!-- Refer character 2198 (著) and 2398 (着) of https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/通用規范漢字表 -->

